            <ArticleTitle>Hemangioblastoma originating from the right cerebellopontine angle.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>372-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The morbidity of hemangioblastoma in the supratentorial region is very low, and is seldom found in the area of the cerebellopontine angle, so it is easily misdiagnosis before surgery. We report and discuss a case of hemangioblastoma originating at the right cerebellopontine angle in a 42-year-old female patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
